          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "reperiō, reperīre — \"to find, to find out, to discover\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Tandem viātōrēs caupōnam reperiunt. At last the travellers find an inn."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "reperiō, reperīre, repperī, repertum. English repertory comes from repertōrium, a list of things found."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "reperiō is built from re- and pariō 'to bring forth, to get' (Lewis & Short): to get again, to find. English repertory and repertoire come from repertōrium, built on it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
