          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: vestīgō, vestīgāre",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "vestīgō, vestīgāre — \"to track, to trace; to search out\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Canis vestīgia lupī in nive vestīgat. The dog tracks the wolf's footprints in the snow."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "vestīgō, vestīgāre, vestīgāvī, vestīgātum. English investigate comes from investīgāre."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "vestīgō goes with vestīgium 'footprint, track'; Lewis & Short call the origin doubtful, so which came first is not settled. English investigate comes from the compound investīgāre."
            }
          ]
        },
